{"name":"Dusky Citron","hex":"#e1c779","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dusky","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Dimly lit, as at dusk (evening).","Having a shade of color that is rather dark."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dusky shark.","A dusky dolphin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dusky"},{"term":"citron","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small citrus tree, Citrus medica.\nThe fruit of a citron tree.\n\nThe candied rind of the citron fruit.\nA greenish yellow colour, inspired by the color of the rind of the citron fruit.","The fruit of a citron tree."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a greenish yellow colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/citron"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dusky","blocks":[{"text":"Dusky is an English electronic music duo from London consisting of Alfie Granger-Howell and Nick Harriman. Formed in 2011, they have released music on various records labels, before setting up their own label 17 Steps in July 2014 with the release of the Love Taking Over EP."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dusky","wikidata":"Q16249370"},{"title":"Citron","blocks":[{"text":"The citron is a large fragrant citrus fruit with a thick, coarse rind. It resembles a lemon, but is larger. It is one of the original citrus fruits from which all other citrus types developed through natural hybrid speciation or artificial hybridization. Though citron cultivars take on a wide variety of physical forms, they are all closely related genetically. It is used in Asian and Mediterranean cuisine, traditional medicines, perfume, and religious rituals and offerings. Hybrids of citrons with other citrus are commercially more prominent, most notably lemons and many limes, which were created using citrons."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Chinesische_Zedrat_Zitrone.jpg/330px-Chinesische_Zedrat_Zitrone.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Citron","wikidata":"Q150064"},{"title":"Citron (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Citron is a dark lemon color similar to that of the fruit citron. As a tertiary color on the RYB color wheel, it is an equal mix of orange and green pigments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Citron.jpg/330px-Citron.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Citron_(color)","wikidata":"Q2974481"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Segment_of_synagogue_mosaic_floor_from_Tiberias_at_Eretz_Israel_Museum_in_Tel_Aviv.jpg/500px-Segment_of_synagogue_mosaic_floor_from_Tiberias_at_Eretz_Israel_Museum_in_Tel_Aviv.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Segment_of_synagogue_mosaic_floor_from_Tiberias_at_Eretz_Israel_Museum_in_Tel_Aviv.jpg/500px-Segment_of_synagogue_mosaic_floor_from_Tiberias_at_Eretz_Israel_Museum_in_Tel_Aviv.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ancient mosaic of Tiberian Synagogue depicting citrons","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASegment_of_synagogue_mosaic_floor_from_Tiberias_at_Eretz_Israel_Museum_in_Tel_Aviv.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/A_species_of_citrus_fruit_%28Citrus_sarcodactylis_Hort._Bog.%29%3B_Wellcome_V0042687.jpg/500px-A_species_of_citrus_fruit_%28Citrus_sarcodactylis_Hort._Bog.%29%3B_Wellcome_V0042687.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/A_species_of_citrus_fruit_%28Citrus_sarcodactylis_Hort._Bog.%29%3B_Wellcome_V0042687.jpg/1280px-A_species_of_citrus_fruit_%28Citrus_sarcodactylis_Hort._Bog.%29%3B_Wellcome_V0042687.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parse